":{"number":"1-0851-4-1","name":"Stupavský potok č. 2","shape":"line","source":"svp","idTok":49024,"boundaryAccuracy":"landmark","verifiedAt":"2026-09-12","checked":{"by":"Claude Code, from the SRZ description","on":"2026-09-12","how":"Desk comparison with the SRZ description, not the water. The SVP Stupavský potok (ID_TOK 49024) ends in the Malina canal, which is exactly where the neighbouring ground 1-0850-4-1 begins ('od ústia do kanála Malina'), so the service's stream is the water the rules book means; this ground is its upper 21.1 km of 27.0, and the 5.9 km below it is that neighbour. The upper end is the springs the description names, which is the far end of the service's line and needs no geocoding. The lower end is the town of Stupava, 0.22 km from the centreline: the safety overflow below the hotel is inside the town and is not a mapped object, so this end is right to a few hundred metres, not to the structure."},"ends":{"start":"landmark: the town of Stupava, 0.22 km from the centreline; the safety overflow itself is not a mapped object","end":"source: the far end of the SVP line ('po pramene')"},"bbox":{"minLat":48.25242432298981,"minLon":17.031376348163356,"maxLat":48.33209760748744,"maxLon":17.181091697477804},"point":{"latitude":48.272002,"longitude":17.120414},"vertices":251}}]}